---
title: "stdlib-totp"
author: bad-antics
date: 2026-04-05
abstract: RFC 6238 TOTP and RFC 4226 HOTP, Google-Authenticator compatible. Covers HOTP counter-based codes, TOTP time-based codes, and verification with a tolerance window.

# HOTP (Counter-based)

HOTP generates a one-time password from a shared secret and a monotonically increasing counter. The same counter must never be reused.

// Generate a 6-digit HOTP code
hotp(secret, 0, 6, "sha1")   // "755224"

// Next counter
hotp(secret, 1, 6, "sha1")   // "287082"

# TOTP (Time-based)

TOTP wraps HOTP using the current Unix time divided by a time step (default 30 seconds). Codes change every step.

// Generate a 6-digit TOTP code for the current time
totp(secret, 6, 30, "sha1")

# Verification

verify_totp checks a user-supplied code against the current window, allowing a small tolerance (±1 step) for clock skew.

// Verify with ±1 step tolerance
verify_totp(secret, code, 6, 30, "sha1", 1)   // true / false

# Canonical Vectors (RFC 6238 Appendix B)

Fixed test vectors for SHA-1 secret "12345678901234567890":

- T=59 -> "287082" (time step 1)
- T=1111111109 -> "081804" (time step 37037036)
- T=1111111111 -> "050471" (time step 37037037)
- T=1234567890 -> "005924" (time step 41152263)
- T=2000000000 -> "279037" (time step 66666666)
- T=20000000000 -> "353130" (time step 666666666)

# Executable Program

fn main() {
    let secret = "12345678901234567890"
    print(totp(secret, 6, 30, "sha1"))
    print(verify_totp(secret, "123456", 6, 30, "sha1", 1))
}

  </script>
  <script src="../ltlml.js"></script>
</body>
